# The variables a program in an hdw4s desktop is handed, by name, one per line.
#
# ONE LIST, TWO READERS. hdw4s-run-session uploads exactly these to the session
# bus, so that a program D-Bus starts gets what it needs; "hdw4s exec" hands a
# command exactly these, taken from the running desktop. A list rather than
# "everything": the session's environment also holds its proxy credential, and
# whatever is uploaded to the bus or given to a command can be read by it.
#
# A line may carry a flag after the name. "display" marks the variables that
# reach the screen and its input; "hdw4s exec" withholds those by default.
# "exec" marks the ones only "hdw4s exec" hands over: the bus knows its own
# address, but a command without it cannot reach the bus -- and "gsettings set"
# then prints an error and EXITS 0, a write that vanished looking like one that
# landed.
DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS exec
USER exec
LOGNAME exec
DISPLAY display
XAUTHORITY display
ICEAUTHORITY display
XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
XDG_SESSION_TYPE
XDG_SESSION_CLASS
XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP
XDG_CONFIG_HOME
XDG_DATA_HOME
XDG_STATE_HOME
XDG_CACHE_HOME
GNOME_SHELL_SESSION_MODE
PATH
HOME
LANG
PULSE_SERVER
PULSE_RUNTIME_PATH
PIPEWIRE_RUNTIME_DIR
GVFS_DISABLE_FUSE
DCONF_PROFILE
